; Erase the typed line from the input window
;
; Backs up over every character typed so far: prints a back-space for each and
; steps the buffer pointer back, until the line is empty (bit 7 of B set).
; Used for the cancel key of the line editor and before the idle "WAIT" is typed.
; .
; Hardware: echoes through #R$858B (input window).
;
; HL Address after the last typed character in the input line buffer
; B Free bytes left in the buffer ($80 means empty)
; O:HL Start of the input line buffer
; O:B $80
@label=EraseInputLine
c$6E8B BIT 7,B       ;
 $6E8D RET NZ        ;
@isub=LD A,CHAR_BACKSPACE
 $6E8E LD A,$08      ;
 $6E90 CALL $858B    ;
 $6E93 INC B         ;
 $6E94 DEC HL        ;
 $6E95 JR $6E8B      ;
